**INTERCEPTA**

Phase 1: mCRPC Ground Truth Specification

*The Exact Numbers Our System Must Reproduce*

Version 1.0 \| March 2026 \| CONFIDENTIAL

Co-Founders: Prasad Akula, MS Bioinformatics & Claude (AI Co-Founder,
Anthropic)

**1. Purpose of This Document**

This document defines the exact clinical trial outcomes that
INTERCEPTA\'s computational engine must reproduce from first principles
during Phase 1 validation. These are our ground truth targets. If our
two-population ODE model, KAALCURA biological axes, and synergy scoring
system can recover these published clinical outcomes computationally, it
proves the engine works. Only then do we trust its novel predictions.

Every number in this document comes from peer-reviewed publications of
the five landmark prostate cancer clinical trials. These are not
approximations. They are the exact values we must match within defined
tolerance bounds.

**2. Validation Principle**

INTERCEPTA follows a strict validation-first methodology: reproduce what
is already known before predicting what is unknown. For Phase 1, this
means:

**Step A:** Model the disease biology of mCRPC using the complete
disease net.

**Step B:** For each clinical trial, simulate the treatment using our
ODE engine with real PK/PD parameters.

**Step C:** Compare simulated survival outcomes to published trial
outcomes.

**Step D:** Quantify the match. If median OS is within ±15% and HR is
within ±20% of published values, the model passes for that trial.

**Step E:** Only after passing all five trials do we trust the engine
for novel drug candidate discovery.

**3. Trial 1: CHAARTED (E3805)**

**3.1 Trial Overview**

**Full Name:** Chemohormonal Therapy Versus Androgen Ablation Randomized
Trial for Extensive Disease in Prostate Cancer

**ClinicalTrials.gov:** NCT00309985

**Publication:** Sweeney et al., NEJM 2015; Long-term: Kyriakopoulos et
al., JCO 2018; 10-year: Annals of Oncology 2025

**Population:** 790 men with metastatic hormone-sensitive prostate
cancer (mHSPC)

**Arms:** ADT + Docetaxel (75 mg/m² q3w × 6 cycles) vs. ADT alone

**Relevance to INTERCEPTA:** Docetaxel targets the proliferating
sensitive cell population. Our model must show that KAALCURA R_prolif
axis identifies docetaxel-sensitive cells, and the ODE engine reproduces
survival benefit in high-volume disease.

**3.2 Ground Truth Numbers**

  ----------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------
  **Endpoint**            **ADT + Docetaxel**     **ADT Alone**

  Median OS (all          57.6 months             44.0 months
  patients)                                       

  HR for death (all       0.61 (95% CI:           Reference
  patients)               0.47--0.80)             

  10-year OS rate         25.9%                   22.5%

  10-year HR              0.78 (p = 0.004)        Reference

  High-volume mOS         \~51 months             \~34 months

  High-volume HR          0.63 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.50--0.79)             

  High-volume 10yr OS     20.9%                   11.4%

  Median time to          20.2 months             11.7 months
  progression                                     

  PSA \< 0.2 at 12 months 27.7%                   16.8%

  PSA \< 0.2 at 6mo → mOS 100.3 months            116.8 months
  ----------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------

**3.3 Key Biological Insight for INTERCEPTA**

CHAARTED demonstrates that docetaxel provides maximal benefit in
high-volume disease (HR 0.63) but limited benefit in low-volume disease.
This is consistent with our two-population model: high-volume disease
has a larger proportion of rapidly proliferating sensitive cells (high
R_prolif), which docetaxel targets effectively. Low-volume disease may
already be enriched for AR-pathway-dependent cells that docetaxel does
not target. Our model must recapitulate this volume-dependent response
pattern.

**4. Trial 2: LATITUDE**

**4.1 Trial Overview**

**Full Name:** Abiraterone Acetate Plus Prednisone in Metastatic,
Castration-Sensitive Prostate Cancer

**ClinicalTrials.gov:** NCT01715285

**Publication:** Fizazi et al., NEJM 2017 (interim); Fizazi et al.,
Lancet Oncol 2019 (final)

**Population:** 1,199 men with newly diagnosed high-risk mCSPC

**Arms:** ADT + Abiraterone (1000 mg daily) + Prednisone (5 mg daily)
vs. ADT + Placebo

**High-risk criteria:** ≥2 of: Gleason ≥8, ≥3 bone lesions, measurable
visceral metastasis

**4.2 Ground Truth Numbers**

  ----------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------
  **Endpoint**            **ADT + Abiraterone**   **ADT + Placebo**

  Median OS (interim,     Not reached             34.7 months
  30.4mo FU)                                      

  HR for death (interim)  0.62 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.51--0.76)             

  Median OS (final,       53.3 months (95% CI:    36.5 months (95% CI:
  51.8mo FU)              48.2--NR)               33.5--40.0)

  HR for death (final)    0.66 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.56--0.78; p\<0.0001)  

  Deaths                  275/597 (46%)           343/602 (57%)

  Median rPFS (interim)   33.0 months             14.8 months

  HR for rPFS             0.47 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.39--0.55)             

  High-volume HR          0.62                    Reference
  (CHAARTED def)                                  
  ----------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------

**4.3 Key Biological Insight for INTERCEPTA**

Abiraterone blocks CYP17A1 in the androgen biosynthesis pathway, cutting
off androgen supply to tumor cells. Unlike docetaxel (which targets
proliferating cells), abiraterone targets the AR-signaling-dependent
population. The similar HR (\~0.62--0.66) to CHAARTED in high-risk
disease suggests that both approaches reduce the sensitive population
but through different mechanisms. Our model must show abiraterone
suppressing the AR-dependent sensitive population while leaving
PARP-dependent or EMT-transitioned resistant cells unaffected.

**5. Trial 3: PROfound**

**5.1 Trial Overview**

**Full Name:** Olaparib for Metastatic Castration-Resistant Prostate
Cancer with HRR Gene Alterations

**ClinicalTrials.gov:** NCT02987543

**Publication:** de Bono et al., NEJM 2020 (rPFS); Hussain et al., NEJM
2020 (OS)

**Population:** 387 men with HRR-mutated mCRPC (Cohort A: BRCA1/2 or
ATM, n=245; Cohort B: other HRR genes, n=142)

**Arms:** Olaparib (300 mg BID) vs. Physician\'s choice of enzalutamide
or abiraterone

**Key feature:** 66--69% crossover from control to olaparib allowed,
diluting observed OS benefit

**5.2 Ground Truth Numbers**

  ----------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------
  **Endpoint**            **Olaparib**            **Control (Enz/Abi)**

  Cohort A median OS      19.1 months (95% CI:    14.7 months (95% CI:
                          17.4--23.4)             11.9--18.8)

  Cohort A HR for death   0.69 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.50--0.97; p=0.02)     

  Crossover-adjusted HR   0.42 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.19--0.91)             

  BRCA-altered rPFS       9.8 months              3.0 months

  BRCA-altered HR (rPFS)  0.22 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.15--0.32)             

  BRCA-altered OS HR      0.63 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.42--0.95)             

  BRCA2 biallelic rPFS    16.6 months (12mo PFS:  \~3.5 months
                          79%)                    

  Cohort A rPFS           7.4 months              3.6 months

  Cohort A HR (rPFS)      0.34 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.25--0.47)             
  ----------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------

**5.3 Key Biological Insight for INTERCEPTA**

PROfound is the critical trial for validating our two-population model.
Olaparib (PARP inhibitor) exploits synthetic lethality in cells with
defective homologous recombination repair (BRCA1/2, ATM mutations).
These are the cells our RNA velocity analysis identifies as
transitioning toward treatment resistance through DNA damage repair
pathway upregulation. In our model, KAALCURA R_ddr (DNA damage repair
axis) must identify the olaparib-sensitive resistant subpopulation. The
crossover-adjusted HR of 0.42 represents the true biological effect
without dilution and is the primary target for our ODE simulation.

**6. Trial 4: PROpel**

**6.1 Trial Overview**

**Full Name:** Olaparib Plus Abiraterone as First-Line Treatment for
Metastatic Castration-Resistant Prostate Cancer

**ClinicalTrials.gov:** NCT03732820

**Publication:** Clarke et al., Lancet Oncol 2023 (final OS)

**Population:** 796 men with first-line mCRPC (unselected for HRR
status)

**Arms:** Olaparib + Abiraterone vs. Placebo + Abiraterone

**6.2 Ground Truth Numbers**

  ----------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------
  **Endpoint**            **Olaparib +            **Placebo +
                          Abiraterone**           Abiraterone**

  Median OS (final)       42.1 months (95% CI:    34.7 months (95% CI:
                          38.4--NR)               31.0--39.3)

  HR for death (final)    0.81 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.67--1.00; p=0.054)    

  Median rPFS             24.8 months             16.6 months
  (investigator)                                  

  HR for rPFS             0.66 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.54--0.81; p\<0.001)   

  BRCA-mutated OS HR      0.29 (95% CI:           Reference
                          0.14--0.56)             
  ----------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------

**6.3 Key Biological Insight for INTERCEPTA**

PROpel tests the exact combination strategy INTERCEPTA\'s architecture
is designed to find: abiraterone kills the AR-dependent sensitive
population, while olaparib targets the BRCA-deficient resistant
population. The overall HR of 0.81 (borderline significance) reflects
dilution from HRR-proficient patients who don\'t benefit from olaparib.
But the BRCA-mutated subgroup HR of 0.29 shows the dramatic combination
effect when the right populations are targeted. This is our model\'s key
prediction: the combination works because it covers BOTH populations
simultaneously. Our synergy scoring (ZIP + Bliss + Loewe + HSA) must
capture this population-level synergy, not just molecular synergy.

**7. Trial 5: TALAPRO-2**

**7.1 Trial Overview**

**Full Name:** Talazoparib Plus Enzalutamide as First-Line Treatment for
Metastatic Castration-Resistant Prostate Cancer

**ClinicalTrials.gov:** NCT03395197

**Publication:** Agarwal et al., Lancet 2023 (rPFS); GU ASCO 2025 (final
OS); Fizazi et al., Nature Med 2024 (HRR cohort)

**Population:** Cohort 1: 805 unselected mCRPC; Cohort 2: 399
HRR-deficient mCRPC

**Arms:** Talazoparib (0.5 mg) + Enzalutamide (160 mg) vs. Placebo +
Enzalutamide

**7.2 Ground Truth Numbers**

  ----------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------
  **Endpoint**            **Talazoparib +         **Placebo +
                          Enzalutamide**          Enzalutamide**

  Cohort 1 Median OS      45.8 months (95% CI:    37.0 months (95% CI:
  (unselected)            39.4--50.8)             34.1--40.4)

  Cohort 1 HR             0.796 (95% CI:          Reference
                          0.661--0.958; p=0.0155) 

  Cohort 2 Median OS      45.1 months (95% CI:    31.1 months (95% CI:
  (HRR-deficient)         35.4--NR)               27.3--35.4)

  Cohort 2 HR             0.622 (95% CI:          Reference
                          0.475--0.814; p=0.0005) 

  Cohort 2 rPFS           30.7 months             12.3 months

  Cohort 2 HR (rPFS)      0.468 (95% CI:          Reference
                          0.359--0.612)           

  BRCA1/2 OS HR           0.497 (95% CI:          Reference
                          0.318--0.776)           

  HRR-nondeficient HR     0.874 (95% CI:          Reference
                          0.711--1.076)           
  ----------------------- ----------------------- -----------------------

**7.3 Key Biological Insight for INTERCEPTA**

TALAPRO-2 is the most recent and arguably most important validation
trial because it demonstrates the PARP inhibitor + AR pathway inhibitor
combination in both HRR-selected and unselected populations. The finding
that median OS is similar across ITT, HRR-deficient, and
HRR-non-deficient subgroups (\~45--47 months) suggests that even
patients without known HRR mutations may harbor subpopulations that
benefit from PARP inhibition. This aligns with INTERCEPTA\'s hypothesis
that RNA velocity can identify treatment-transitioning cell populations
that standard genomic testing misses. Our model must reproduce: (a) the
\~8.8 month OS improvement in unselected patients, (b) the 14-month
improvement in HRR-deficient patients, and (c) the attenuated benefit in
HRR-nondeficient patients.

**8. Validation Success Criteria**

For INTERCEPTA Phase 1 to be considered validated, the computational
engine must meet ALL of the following criteria:

**8.1 Primary Validation Metrics**

  ----------------- ----------------- ------------------ ------------------
  **Trial**         **Metric**        **Published        **Acceptable
                                      Value**            Range**

  CHAARTED          High-volume HR    0.63               0.50 -- 0.76

  LATITUDE          Final OS HR       0.66               0.53 -- 0.79

  PROfound          Cohort A OS HR    0.69               0.55 -- 0.83

  PROpel            BRCA OS HR        0.29               0.23 -- 0.35

  TALAPRO-2         Cohort 2 OS HR    0.622              0.50 -- 0.75
  ----------------- ----------------- ------------------ ------------------

**8.2 Secondary Validation Metrics**

The model must also correctly reproduce qualitative patterns: (a)
CHAARTED shows volume-dependent benefit --- high-volume HR \< low-volume
HR, (b) PROfound shows BRCA2 \> ATM benefit, (c) PROpel shows
BRCA-subgroup dramatically better than ITT, (d) TALAPRO-2 shows
HRR-deficient \> HRR-nondeficient benefit, (e) all trials: sensitive
population declines faster with treatment, resistant population emerges
over time without combination therapy.

**8.3 Model Failure Criteria**

The model FAILS validation if any of the following occur: (a) any
primary HR falls outside the acceptable range, (b) the qualitative
volume/mutation-dependent patterns are reversed, (c) the two-population
dynamics show resistant cell resurgence in combination therapy when the
clinical trial shows durable response, (d) the synergy score for PROpel
or TALAPRO-2 combinations shows antagonism when clinical data shows
synergy.

